Killing always-peaceful humans (minetown watch, shopkeepers, priests -
even crossaligned ones) gives you the "You murderer!" message,
regardless of race or alignment. Every time you get that message, you
get a -2 luck penalty and lose intrinsic telepathy if you had it.
That's why I usually try to level up my starting pet and have it do
the dirty work on the regular watchmen first, and then let it fight
the watch captain and heal it if I can (attack or throw a healing
potion at it if I can't cast it), and use /oSpeed Monster and /oMake
Invis on it if I have them. If you must kill them yourself, use a
stethoscope to check your alignment afterwards. Later in the game if I
want to kill them I will usually polytrap dance with any pet until I
have something decent, something like a giant or an elemental is
usually sufficient, doesn't need to be anything crazy.

One other thing to note, watchmen follow you down stairs so you can
strand the non captain watch on the level below so you don't have to
kill them.

